#import "/formatting.typ": *

#show: recipe.with(title: "Lemon Pound Cake", yield: "1 loaf")[
  Dry:
  - 180g all-purpose flour #aside[340mℓ]
  - 1.5g baking soda #aside[1.2mℓ]
  - 1.5g salt #aside[1.2mℓ]

  Wet:
  - 113g butter #aside[1 stick]
  - 300g sugar #pause[340mℓ]
  - 150g eggs #pause[3 large]
  - 40g lemon juice #aside[38mℓ]
  - 5g lemon zest, grated #pause[9mℓ]

  Extra:
  - 113g sour cream #aside[114mℓ]
  - 100g @R_lemon-glaze[lemon glaze]
]

0. RETRIEVE butter & eggs from refrigeration. Rest until room temperature #pause[\~1-2
    hours]
+ PREHEAT oven, 180°C #aside[350°F]
+ SIFT dry ingredients into medium bowl.
+ MIX wet ingredients separately, medium speed:~
  + Butter & sugar. #aside[8-10 minutes]
  + Eggs. #aside[one at a time, until combined]
  + Lemon juice & lemon zest. #aside[until combined]
+ SWAP mixer attachment for Dutch hook.
+ MIX into wet ingredients, low speed: dry ingredients; sour cream.
+ GREASE a 9"×5" loaf pan.#footnote[The original recipe suggests a 10-12 cup Bundt pan may
    work better for two loaves.]
+ POUR batter into loaf pans.
+ BAKE covered, until knife tests clean. #pause[\~1 hour]
+ COOL within loaf pan. #pause[\~15 min.]
+ TRANSFER to flat surface.
+ COAT with glaze.
+ COVER airtight, and possibly refrigerate or freeze#footnote[~It should be possible to
    freeze this cake for up to 3 months.], until ready to serve.
